tion (Rezende et al., 2014; Kingma and Welling, 2014). Based on the central limit theorem, $\mathcal{N}(\mu = \lambda, \sigma^2 = \lambda)$ can approximate Poisson $(\lambda)$ . Thus, we sample from the Poisson distribution directly to avoid the issue of discretization and use the Gaussian distribution as an approximation when calculating the Poisson distribution's gradient. Particularly, the reparameterization of a Gaussian distribution $x \sim \mathcal{N}(\mu, \sigma^2)$ is $x = \mu + \epsilon \cdot \sigma$ , $\epsilon \sim \mathcal{N}(0,1)$ .

